{title: Just as I Am}
{artist: Charlotte Elliott (1789-1871)}
{key: Eb}
{copyright: Public Domain}

{sov: Verse 1}
[Eb]Just as I am, with[Bb]out one plea,
But [Bb]that Thy blood was [Eb]shed for me,
And [Eb]that Thou bidd’st me [Ab]come to Thee,
O [Eb]Lamb of God, I [Bb]come, I [Eb]come.
{eov}

{sov: Verse 2}
[Eb]Just as I am, and [Bb]waiting not
To [Bb]rid my soul of [Eb]one dark blot,
To [Eb]Thee whose blood can [Ab]cleanse each spot,
O [Eb]Lamb of God, I [Bb]come, I [Eb]come.
{eov}

{sov: Verse 3}
[Eb]Just as I am, though [Bb]tossed about
With [Bb]many a conflict, [Eb]many a doubt,
[Eb]Fightings and fears with[Ab]in, without,
O [Eb]Lamb of God, I [Bb]come, I [Eb]come.
{eov}

{sov: Verse 4}
[Eb]Just as I am, Thy [Bb]love unknown
Hath [Bb]broken every [Eb]barrier down;
Now, [Eb]to be Thine, yea, [Ab]Thine alone,
O [Eb]Lamb of God, I [Bb]come, I [Eb]come.
{eov}
